CORE
main.sh

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
"$@" in an assignment joins the fields with the first byte of IFS in
dash, busybox and zsh and with a space in bash and mksh, which agree
with the default IFS. Assignments to _, which bash overwrites after each
command, are allowed; reading it is not.
